    "body": "## Summary\n\n- `M-x` still hung Emacs (CPU at 98%) and the dotted line wrapped in a small frame, so `sp-mini-frame` goes back to its original plain setup from before the nano rework (#114/#115).\n- Removed: the nano-style `M-x` prompt, the dotted line, the colour handling (#121/#123), the dimming for note functions, and every function-computed frame parameter.\n- Kept from the sizing work: centred horizontally and vertically, 4 pixels of padding, and a fixed height of 17 lines for the 13 `vertico-count` candidates (the prompt and 13 lines, made taller by the larger minibuffer text), so there is no long blank box. `mini-frame-resize` stays `not-set`.\n- Original dimming for `find-file`, `vulpea-find` and `org-node-find` is back as it was.\n- Docs (`sp-mini-frame.org`, the dividers guide, `sp-nano-style.org`) and CHANGELOG updated.\n\n## Not tested\n\n- Not run in Emacs (none in the container).\n- If the hang persists with this plain setup, the cause is not in `sp-mini-frame`; the original dimming (loops over `face-list`) is the only remaining code of its own.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01MfEFZ7KDkwwcifErLfjf4X)_",
